  "id": "COMPOUND:20311 - PROTEIN:5003",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Pantetheine and ME-180, through a series of target interactions involving Phosphodiesterase 6C. Pantetheine is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including quianhucoumarin D and (4S)-1-methyl-4-prop-1-en-2-ylcyclohexene;sulfane, which in turn target ME-180. These compounds are likely acting through a common pathway, possibly by inhibiting Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is a key enzyme in the regulation of intracellular cyclic AMP levels. The presence of multiple distinct but related compounds targeting the same enzyme supports the idea that Pantetheine may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C in a manner that could influence ME-180 activity. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust and reliable mechanistic relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact mode of action and the biological relevance of this interaction.",
